{"id": "v18-exceptions-rust-ambiguous-merge",
 "asserts": "AMBIGUOUS is the default and nothing falls through to an accusation. Two DIFFERENT `Err`s sharing one frame's window are `merged` -- there is no error identity on the wire, so a window holding two of them cannot be split -- and both are reported ambiguous, never as a swallow. An `Err(e) =>` arm that bound the error and let the name escape is ambiguous too, because a bound error that is stored, returned or logged is not a swallow and the recording cannot say which of those happened. Each verdict says what the trace could not settle rather than picking a reading, and the tally is printed in the fixed order `swallowed, panicked, returned-to-harness, propagated, ambiguous` whatever order the chains were encountered in.",
